<template>
<role>Takes a list of user form inputs about a game setting in xml format and fills in the empty fields.</role>
    
<systemPrompt>
You are a specialized prompt generator for creating interesting and unique roleplaying game worlds of all kinds. You will be provided with an XML structure representing a game setting, which may have some fields filled in and others left empty. Your task is to intelligently fill in the empty fields based on the context provided by the filled fields, ensuring that the completed XML is coherent and consistent. Use multiple (3-5) paragraphs in the description field to provide a rich and immersive overview of the setting.
</systemPrompt>

<generationPrompt>
Here is the XML structure representing the game setting:

<setting>
  <name>{{ setting.name }}</name>
  {% if setting.description %}
  <description>{{ setting.description }}</description>
  {% else %}
  <description><!-- use several paragraphs to provide a rich and immersive overview of the setting --></description>
  {% endif %}
  <theme>{{ setting.theme }}</theme>
  <genre>{{ setting.genre }}</genre>
  <startingLocationType>{{ setting.startingLocationType }}</startingLocationType>
  <magicLevel>{{ setting.magicLevel }}</magicLevel>
  <techLevel>{{ setting.techLevel }}</techLevel>
  <tone>{{ setting.tone }}</tone>
  <difficulty>{{ setting.difficulty }}</difficulty>
  <currencyName>{{ setting.currencyName }}</currencyName>
  <currencyNamePlural>{{ setting.currencyNamePlural }}</currencyNamePlural>
  <currencyValueNotes>{{ setting.currencyValueNotes }}</currencyValueNotes>
  <writingStyleNotes>{{ setting.writingStyleNotes }}</writingStyleNotes>
  <baseContextPreamble>{{ setting.baseContextPreamble }}</baseContextPreamble>
  {% if setting.characterGenInstructions %}
  <characterGenInstructions>{{ setting.characterGenInstructions }}</characterGenInstructions>
  {% else %}
  <characterGenInstructions><!-- Provide instructions to the LLM for generating NPCs in this setting --></characterGenInstructions>
  {% endif %}
  <playerStartingLevel>{{ setting.playerStartingLevel }}</playerStartingLevel>
  <defaultPlayerName>{{ setting.defaultPlayerName }}</defaultPlayerName>
  <defaultPlayerDescription>{{ setting.defaultPlayerDescription }}</defaultPlayerDescription>
  <defaultStartingLocation>{{ setting.defaultStartingLocation }}</defaultStartingLocation>
  <defaultStartingCurrency>{{ setting.defaultStartingCurrency }}</defaultStartingCurrency>
  <defaultExistingSkills>
    <!-- Baseline skills list. When completing the XML, add up to 10 additional skills that are specific to this setting (technology, magic, psionics, etc.). Avoid repeating or replacing the existing skills and keep the additions focused on missing niches. Names only, inside <skill></skill> tags. -->
{% for skill in setting.defaultExistingSkills %}
    <skill>{{ skill }}</skill>
{% endfor %}
  </defaultExistingSkills>
  <hidingAttribute>{{ setting.hidingAttribute }}</hidingAttribute>
  <hidingSkill>{{ setting.hidingSkill }}</hidingSkill>
  <perceptionAttribute>{{ setting.perceptionAttribute }}</perceptionAttribute>
  <perceptionSkill>{{ setting.perceptionSkill }}</perceptionSkill>
  <availableClasses>
    <!-- A list of classes that the player can choose from. These should be appropriate to the setting and the player's background. Names only, inside <class></class> tags-->
{% for cls in setting.availableClasses %}
    <class>{{ cls }}</class>
{% endfor %}
  </availableClasses>
  <availableRaces>
    <!-- A list of races that the player can choose from. These should be appropriate to the setting and the player's background. Names only, inside <race></race> tags-->
{% for race in setting.availableRaces %}
    <race>{{ race }}</race>
{% endfor %}
  </availableRaces>
</setting>
{% if attributeOptions and attributeOptions.length %}

Available attribute options for hidingAttribute and perceptionAttribute. Use the exact <name> value in the completed XML:
<availableCheckAttributes>
{% for attribute in attributeOptions %}
  <attribute>
    <name>{{ attribute.name }}</name>
    <label>{{ attribute.label }}</label>
    <description>{{ attribute.description }}</description>
  </attribute>
{% endfor %}
</availableCheckAttributes>
{% endif %}

Fill in any empty fields with appropriate values that fit the context of the filled fields. Ensure that the completed XML is well-formed and adheres to the structure provided. Do not alter any fields that are already filled in, except for defaultExistingSkills where you should add up to 10 setting-specific skills that are missing.
When filling hidingAttribute and perceptionAttribute, use exact names from the available attribute options. When filling hidingSkill and perceptionSkill, choose exact names from defaultExistingSkills or leave the field empty when no skill is needed.
{% if hasImage %}Use the uploaded image as the primary reference and fill in the missing fields to generate the setting depicted in the image, aligning details like tone, technology, and atmosphere with what you see.{% endif %}
Return only the completed XML structure without any additional commentary or explanation. The available setting fields are: name, description, theme, genre, startingLocationType, magicLevel, techLevel, tone, difficulty, currencyName, currencyNamePlural, currencyValueNotes, writingStyleNotes, baseContextPreamble, characterGenInstructions, playerStartingLevel, defaultPlayerName, defaultPlayerDescription, defaultStartingLocation, defaultStartingCurrency, defaultExistingSkills, hidingAttribute, hidingSkill, perceptionAttribute, perceptionSkill, availableClasses, availableRaces, and customSlopWords.

When filling defaultStartingLocation, prefer this suggested multi-line format (with blank lines between lines):
Region name: [name]

Summary: [description]

Rooms/Locations: [comma-separated list of rooms]

Region exits: [comma-separated list of connected regions]

When filling baseContextPreamble, use the exact single-line bracketed format shown on the form, like:
[Title: The Verdant Metropolis; Tags: heroic, dark, edgy; Genre: sci-fi, adventure, dystopian]

When populating currencyValueNotes, describe the relative value of the currency in terms of common goods and services in the setting, using 5 or 6 entries ordered from cheapest to most expensive with the format:

[value]: [item]
[value]: [item]
...

{% if additionalInstructions %}Additional instructions from the user:
{{ additionalInstructions }}{% endif %}
</generationPrompt>
</template>
